    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d60">

                <pb facs="0103" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg85"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation (3A)/10–446</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the President of the Emergency Advisory Committee for Political Defense</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Guani</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-10-31">October 31, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge your
                    Excellency’s communication of October 4, 1946,<anchor n="17" xml:id="d60-f1"/>
                    concerning the need to prevent dangerous Axis elements from entering the Western
                    Hemispheres especially from neutral countries, together with the attached
                    preliminary list of such persons heretofore in Spanish territory.</p>
                <p>The Government of the United States welcomes the initiative taken by the
                    Emergency Advisory Committee for Political Defense concerning this subject, and
                    will be entirely disposed to cooperate in preventive action, in concert with the
                    other American Republics, along the lines of the recommendations made by the
                    Committee.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> F. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
